      "answer": "The Gulfstream G700 and Bombardier Global 7500 are both top contenders in the ultra-long-range business jet category, each with distinct advantages. Here’s a comparison based on key operational metrics:\n\nRange \n- Gulfstream G700: Approximately 7,750 nautical miles \n- Bombardier Global 7500: Approximately 7,700 nautical miles \n\nPassengers \n- Gulfstream G700: Accommodates up to 14 passengers with flexible living areas \n- Bombardier Global 7500: Seats up to 19 passengers, offering customizable layouts \n\nCruise Speed \n- Gulfstream G700: Maximum cruise speed of Mach 0.935 \n- Bombardier Global 7500: Maximum cruise speed of Mach 0.925 \n\nCabin Characteristics \n- Gulfstream G700: Features a longer cabin at 56 ft 11 in and wider at 8 ft 2 in, allowing for up to five living areas \n- Bombardier Global 7500: Offers a four-zone cabin with a dedicated master suite and innovative Nuage seating for enhanced comfort \n\nMission Strengths \n- Gulfstream G700: Slightly faster and more versatile cabin layout, ideal for those prioritizing space and adaptability \n- Bombardier Global 7500: Exceptional range and higher passenger capacity, catering to corporate clients and luxury travelers \n\nBoth jets excel in luxury, comfort, and performance, making your choice dependent on specific mission requirements, cabin preferences, and budget considerations. \n\n✅ GOOD FIT",
